# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and check it back out as
# LF on every platform, overriding whatever core.autocrlf is set to locally.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree on
# Windows while .prettierrc requires "endOfLine": "lf" — so every file fails
# the linter immediately after a clone, and the suite only passes on Linux.
# Declaring the convention in the repository keeps it independent of each
# developer's global Git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: left byte-for-byte, never line-ending converted, regardless of
# what Git's text/binary heuristic would guess. None are tracked today; this
# is here so the first image or PDF added does not get mangled.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
